Z||000000||Homicidal||09-18-2000||01:45 AM||||It was that time once again.  I felt the bowel movements and it was time to hit the can.  But not without appropriate reading material of course!  So in the mad rush of getting to the holy seat I grab a copy of the latest issue of Automobile with that beautiful yellow Ferrari on the cover.<P>I sit, relax, and open the magazine.  A small article catches my eye with the letters: <B>88' Fiero</B> wonderfully gracing the thin, otherwise rather bland page of this magazine.  I of course get giddy and I turn the page quickly to see if I can find some pics of our plastic beauties.  I found one alright:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/master_sushi2000/fiero.jpg"> <P>My stomach (along with other things) dropped.  I couldn't beleive I was actually holding this blasphamous object.  I quickly turned back to the start of the article to see the rest of the bashing.  <P>Whoever this writer is needs a massive cranial adjustment ala' a HAMMER.  <P>Sad thing is, he actually has driven the car many times (so he says) and this is what he writes:<P><B>"My own experiences with Fieros include driving the new ones each year from 1984 to 1988 and wondering how they could continue to be so uniformly substandard."</B><P>GRR.  What really peeves me is this though (paraphrased):<P><B>"I should also point out every Fiero I see seems to be winking at me.  It's true!  Everyu Fiero I have seen driving around has one headlight up and one down.  Is this some Tribal thing?  Is it a secret to other Fiero owners announcing the time and place of the mid-engined plastic bodied revolution that will once and for all destroy the old automotive order?  Or do the headlights just not work properly?"  </B><P>The rest is history.  <P>Man, what is wrong with this SOB?  I don't know where he lives, but every Fiero I have seen, only 2 have had BOTH their headlights up.  Why does he insist on using such a childing, almost jealous like bash?  Just so sad.... <P>I wasn't really angry when I saw this article, but I was REALLY angry when I held this peice of $hit in my hands.  <P>It will be burned shortly.  But first I must peel out on it.||||reg||8
